G4314.b:
⟪πρός⟫, prep. c. gen., dat., acc.
⟪I.⟫ C. gen., of motion from a place, ⟪from the side of⟫, hence metaph., ⟪in the interests of⟫, ⟦Acts 27:34|Ac 27:34⟧ (cf. Page, in l.).
⟪II.⟫ C. dat., of local proximity, ⟪hard by⟫, ⟪near⟫, ⟪at⟫: ⟦Mark 5:11|Mk 5:11⟧, ⟦Luke 19:37|Lk 19:37⟧, ⟦John 18:16|Jo 18:16⟧ ⟦John 20:11|20:11⟧, ⟦John 20:12|12⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:13|Re 1:13⟧.
⟪III.⟫ C. acc., of motion or direction towards a place or object, ⟪to⟫, ⟪towards⟫.
	⟪1.⟫ Of place,
		⟪(a)⟫ after verbs of motion or of speaking and other words with the idea of direction: ἔρχομαι, ἀναβαίνω, πορεύομαι, λέγω, ἐπιστολή, etc., ⟦Matthew 3:14|Mt 3:14⟧, ⟦Mark 6:51|Mk 6:51⟧, ⟦Luke 11:5|Lk 11:5⟧, ⟦John 2:3|Jo 2:3⟧, ⟦Acts 9:2|Ac 9:2⟧, al. mult.; metaph., of mental direction, hostile or otherwise, ⟦Luke 23:12|Lk 23:12⟧, ⟦John 6:52|Jo 6:52⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 7:4|II Co 7:4⟧, ⟦Ephesians 6:12|Eph 6:12⟧, ⟦Colossians 3:13|Col 3:13⟧, al.; of the issue or end, ⟦Luke 14:32|Lk 14:32⟧, ⟦John 11:4|Jo 11:4⟧, al.; of purpose, ⟦Matthew 26:12|Mt 26:12⟧, ⟦Romans 3:26|Ro 3:26⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 6:5|I Co 6:5⟧, al.; πρὸς τό, c. inf., denoting purpose (cf. M, Pr., 218, 220; Lft., Notes, 131), ⟦Matthew 5:28|Mt 5:28⟧, ⟦Mark 13:22|Mk 13:22⟧, ⟦Ephesians 6:11|Eph 6:11⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:9|I Th 2:9⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ of close proximity, ⟪at⟫, by, ⟪with⟫: ⟦Matthew 3:10|Mt 3:10⟧, ⟦Mark 11:4|Mk 11:4⟧, ⟦Luke 4:11|Lk 4:11⟧, ⟦Acts 3:2|Ac 3:2⟧, al.; after εἶναι, ⟦Matthew 13:56|Mt 13:56⟧, ⟦Mark 6:3|Mk 6:3⟧, ⟦John 1:1|Jo 1:1⟧, al.
	⟪2.⟫ Of time,
		⟪(a)⟫ ⟪towards⟫ (Plat., Xen., LXX: ⟦Genesis 8:11|Ge 8:11⟧, al.): ⟦Luke 24:29|Lk 24:29⟧;
		⟪(b)⟫ ⟪for⟫: πρὸς καιρόν, ⟦Luke 8:13|Lk 8:13⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:5|I Co 7:5⟧; πρὸς ὥραν, ⟦John 5:35|Jo 5:35⟧, al.; πρὸς ὀλίγον, ⟦James 4:14|Ja 4:14⟧.
	⟪3.⟫ Of relation
		⟪(a)⟫ ⟪toward⟫, ⟪with⟫: ⟦Romans 5:1|Ro 5:1⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 1:12|II Co 1:12⟧, ⟦Colossians 4:5|Col 4:5⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 4:12|I Th 4:12⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ ⟪with regard to⟫: ⟦Matthew 19:8|Mt 19:8⟧, ⟦Mark 12:12|Mk 12:12⟧, ⟦Romans 8:31|Ro 8:31⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ ⟪pertaining to⟫, ⟪to⟫: ⟦Matthew 27:4|Mt 27:4⟧, ⟦John 21:22|Jo 21:22⟧, ⟦Romans 15:17|Ro 15:17⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:17|He 2:17⟧ ⟦Hebrews 5:1|5:1⟧;
		⟪(d)⟫ ⟪according to⟫: ⟦Luke 12:47|Lk 12:47⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 5:10|II Co 5:10⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:14|Ga 2:14⟧, ⟦Ephesians 3:4|Eph 3:4⟧ ⟦Ephesians 4:14|4:14⟧;
		⟪(e)⟫ ⟪in comparison with⟫: ⟦Romans 8:18|Ro 8:18⟧.
⟪IV.⟫ In composition: ⟪towards⟫ (προσέρχομαι), ⟪to⟫ (προσάγω), ⟪against⟫ (προσκόπτω), ⟪besides⟫ (προσδαπανάω).

G4323.b:
* ⟪προσ-ανα-τίθημι⟫, ⟪to lay on⟫ or ⟪offer besides⟫; mid.,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to lay on oneself in addition⟫, ⟪undertake besides⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ c. gen. pers., of giving or obtaining information, ⟪to consult⟫, ⟪communicate⟫: ⟦Galatians 1:16|Ga 1:16⟧ ⟦Galatians 2:6|2:6⟧ (Lft., in l.; cf. ἀνα-τίθημι).

G4352.b:
⟪προσ-κυνέω⟫, -ῶ
(< κυνέω, to kiss), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨שׁחה⁩ hith.;] ⟪to make obeisance⟫, ⟪do reverence to⟫, ⟪worship⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ prop. (as in cl., of the gods: Hdt., Æsch., Plat., al.), of God, Christ and supra-mundane beings: absol., ⟦John 4:20|Jo 4:20⟧ ⟦John 12:20|12:20⟧, ⟦Acts 8:27|Ac 8:27⟧ ⟦Acts 24:11|24:11⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:21|He 11:21⟧ (Westc., in l.), ⟦Revelation 11:1|Re 11:1⟧; πίπτειν καὶ π., ⟦Revelation 5:14|Re 5:14⟧; c. dat. (of the significance of this constr. as compared with the usual cl., c. acc., v. Abbott, JG, 78 f.; JV, 133 ff.), ⟦John 4:21|Jo 4:21⟧, ⟦John 4:23|23⟧, ⟦Acts 7:43|Ac 7:43⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:25|I Co 14:25⟧, ⟦Hebrews 1:6|He 1:6⟧, ⟦Revelation 4:10|Re 4:10⟧ ⟦Revelation 7:11|7:11⟧ ⟦Revelation 11:16|11:16⟧ ⟦Revelation 13:4|13:4⟧, ⟦Revelation 13:15|15⟧ ⟦Revelation 14:7|14:7⟧ ⟦Revelation 16:2|16:2⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:4|19:4⟧, ⟦Revelation 19:10|10⟧, ⟦Revelation 19:20|20⟧ ⟦Revelation 22:8|22:8⟧, ⟦Revelation 22:9|9⟧; c. acc. (v. supr.), ⟦Matthew 4:10|Mt 4:10⟧, ⟦Luke 4:8|Lk 4:8⟧ ⟦Luke 24:52|24:52⟧ (WH, R, mg., om.), ⟦John 4:22|Jo 4:22⟧, ⟦John 4:24|24⟧, ⟦Revelation 9:20|Re 9:20⟧ ⟦Revelation 13:4|13:4⟧, ⟦Revelation 13:8|8⟧, ⟦Revelation 13:12|12⟧ ⟦Revelation 14:9|14:9⟧, ⟦Revelation 14:11|11⟧ ⟦Revelation 20:4|20:4⟧; seq. ἐπώπιον, ⟦Luke 4:7|Lk 4:7⟧, ⟦Revelation 15:4|Re 15:4⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ as in cl., of homage to human superiors (cf. MM, xxi): absol., ⟦Matthew 20:20|Mt 20:20⟧, ⟦Acts 10:25|Ac 10:25⟧; c. dat. (v. supr.), ⟦Matthew 2:2|Mt 2:2⟧, ⟦Matthew 2:8|8⟧ ⟦Matthew 8:2|8:2⟧ ⟦Matthew 9:18|9:18⟧ ⟦Matthew 14:33|14:33⟧ ⟦Matthew 15:25|15:25⟧ ⟦Matthew 18:26|18:26⟧ ⟦Matthew 28:9|28:9⟧, ⟦Mark 15:19|Mk 15:19⟧, ⟦John 9:38|Jo 9:38⟧; πεσὼν π., ⟦Matthew 2:11|Mt 2:11⟧ ⟦Matthew 4:9|4:9⟧; ἐνώπιον τ. ποδῶν, ⟦Revelation 3:9|Re 3:9⟧; c. acc., ⟦Mark 5:6|Mk 5:6⟧ (dat. T).†

G4355.b:
⟪προσ-λαμβάνω⟫,
[in LXX: ⟦Psalms 18:16|Ps 117 (18):16⟧ (⁨משׁה⁩ hi.), ⟦Psalms 73:24|Ps 72 (73):24⟧ (⁨לקח⁩), etc.;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to take in addition⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to take to oneself⟫, ⟪take⟫, ⟪receive⟫; in NT always mid., -ομαι;
	⟪(a)⟫ of things: of food, c. acc., ⟦Acts 27:33|Ac 27:33⟧; c. gen. part., ⟦Acts 27:36|Ac 27:36⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of persons: c. acc., ⟦Matthew 16:22|Mt 16:22⟧, ⟦Mark 8:32|Mk 8:32⟧ (v. Swete, in l.), ⟦Acts 17:5|Ac 17:5⟧ ⟦Acts 18:26|18:26⟧ ⟦Acts 28:2|28:2⟧, ⟦Romans 14:1|Ro 14:1⟧, ⟦Romans 14:3|3⟧ ⟦Romans 15:7|15:7⟧, ⟦Philemon 1:17|Phm 17⟧.†

G4366.b:
**† ⟪προσ-ρήγνυμι⟫,
[in Aq.: ⟦Psalms 2:9|Ps 2:9⟧*;] ⟪to break against⟫, ⟪dash against⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ trans. (παιδία πέτραις, FlJ, Ant., ix, 4, 6);
⟪(b)⟫ intrans., c. dat.: ⟦Luke 6:48|Lk 6:48⟧, ⟦Luke 6:49|49⟧ (cf. προσπίπτω).†

G4383.b:
⟪πρόσωπον⟫, -ου, τό
(< πρός, ὤψ), [in LXX chiefly and very freq. for ⁨פָּנִים⁩;]
⟪1.⟫ prop., of persons (so always in cl.);
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪the face⟫, ⟪countenance⟫: ⟦Matthew 6:16|Mt 6:16⟧, ⟦Matthew 6:17|17⟧, ⟦Mark 14:65|Mk 14:65⟧, ⟦Luke 9:29|Lk 9:29⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 3:7|II Co 3:7⟧, ⟦Revelation 4:7|Re 4:7⟧, al.; τὸ π. τῆς γενέσεως (EV, natural face), ⟦James 1:23|Ja 1:23⟧; πίπτειν ἐπὶ (τὰ) π., ⟦Matthew 17:6|Mt 17:6⟧, ⟦Luke 5:12|Lk 5:12⟧, ⟦Revelation 7:11|Re 7:11⟧, al.; ἀγνοούμενος τῷ π., ⟦Galatians 1:22|Ga 1:22⟧; π., οὐ καρδίᾳ, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:17|I Th 2:17⟧; κατὰ πρόσωπον (in front, facing: Thuc., Xen., al.), ⟪when present⟫, ⟪face to face⟫, ⟦Acts 25:16|Ac 25:16⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:1|II Co 10:1⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:7|7⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:11|Ga 2:11⟧; id. c. gen., as compound prep., ⟪in the presence of⟫ (not cl.; v. Bl., § 40, 9; M, Pr., 99 f.; Thackeray, Gr., 43 f.), ⟦Luke 2:31|Lk 2:31⟧, ⟦Acts 3:13|Ac 3:13⟧; similarly ἀπὸ π. (Heb. ⁨מִלִּפְּנֵי⁩; v. Dalman, Words, 29), ⟪from the presence of⟫, ⟦Acts 3:19|Ac 3:19⟧ ⟦Acts 5:41|5:41⟧ ⟦Acts 7:45|7:45⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 1:9|II Th 1:9⟧, ⟦Revelation 12:14|Re 12:14⟧ ⟦Revelation 20:11|20:11⟧; πρὸ π. (Heb. ⁨לִפְנֵי⁩), ⟪before⟫, ⟦Matthew 11:10|Mt 11:10⟧, ⟦Mark 1:2|Mk 1:2⟧, ⟦Luke 7:27|Lk 7:27⟧(LXX), al.; in other phrases resembling Heb. idiom (Thackeray, Gr., 42), βλέπειν (ὁρᾶν, θεωρεῖν, ἰδεῖν) τὸ π., ⟪to see one's face⟫, i.e. see him in person, ⟦Matthew 18:10|Mt 18:10⟧, ⟦Acts 20:25|Ac 20:25⟧, ⟦Acts 20:38|38⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:10|I Th 3:10⟧, ⟦Revelation 22:4|Re 22:4⟧; ἐμφανισθῆναι τῷ π. τοῦ θεοῦ, ⟦Hebrews 9:24|He 9:24⟧; ἐν π. Χριστοῦ, ⟦2 Corinthians 2:10|II Co 2:10⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 4:6|4:6⟧; μετὰ τοῦ π. σου, ⟪with thy presence⟫, ⟦Acts 2:28|Ac 2:28⟧(LXX); εἰς π. τῶν ἐκκλησιῶν, ⟦2 Corinthians 8:24|II Co 8:24⟧; στηρίζειν τὸ π. (Heb. ⁨שׂוּם⁩ ⁨פָּנִים⁩: ⟦Jeremiah 21:10|Je 21:10⟧, al.; v. Dalman, Words, 30), c. inf., ⟪to set one's face towards⟫, ⟦Luke 9:51|Lk 9:51⟧; similarly, τὸ π. αὐτοῦ ἦν πορευόμενον (op. cit., 31), ⟦Luke 9:53|Lk 9:53⟧; τὸ π. τοῦ κυρίου ἐπί, ⟦1 Peter 3:12|I Pe 3:12⟧(LXX);
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪form⟫, ⟪person⟫: καυχᾶσθαι ἐν π. καὶ μὴ ἐν καρδίᾳ, ⟦2 Corinthians 5:12|II Co 5:12⟧ (cf. ⟦1 Samuel 16:7|I Ki 16:7⟧); metaph., as in Heb. idiom, of judgment according to appearance, external condition or circumstances (⁨נשָׂאָ⁩probably misspelled נָשָׂא ⁨פָּנִים⁩; v. Dalman, Words, 30; Thackeray, Gr., 43 f.): λαμβάνειν π., ⟦Luke 20:21|Lk 20:21⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:6|Ga 2:6⟧; βλέπειν εἰς π., ⟦Matthew 22:16|Mt 22:16⟧, ⟦Mark 12:14|Mk 12:14⟧; θαυμάζειν πρόσωπα, ⟦Jude 1:16|Ju 16⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Of things (cf. Dalman, Words, 30);
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪face⟫, ⟪appearance⟫ (⟦Psalms 104:30|Ps 103 (104):30⟧): ⟦Matthew 16:3|Mt 16:3⟧ (WH, R, mg., om.), ⟦Luke 12:56|Lk 12:56⟧, ⟦James 1:11|Ja 1:11⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪surface⟫ (⟦Genesis 2:6|Ge 2:6⟧): ⟦Luke 21:35|Lk 21:35⟧, ⟦Acts 17:26|Ac 17:26⟧.

G4396.b:
⟪προφήτης⟫, -ου, ὁ [< πρόφημι, to speak forth),
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨נָבִיא⁩;] one who acts as an interpreter or forth-teller of the Divine will (v. Lft., Notes, 83 f.; Tr., Syn., § vi), ⟪a prophet⟫;
⟪1.⟫ in cl. (Æsch., Hdt., Plat., al.), of the interpreters of oracles.
⟪2.⟫ In NT,
	⟪(a)⟫ of the OT prophets: ⟦Matthew 5:12|Mt 5:12⟧, ⟦Mark 6:15|Mk 6:15⟧, ⟦Luke 4:27|Lk 4:27⟧, ⟦John 8:52|Jo 8:52⟧, ⟦Romans 11:3|Ro 11:3⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ of prophets in general: ⟦Matthew 10:41|Mt 10:41⟧ ⟦Matthew 13:57|13:57⟧ ⟦Matthew 21:46|21:46⟧, ⟦Mark 6:4|Mk 6:4⟧, ⟦Luke 13:33|Lk 13:33⟧, al.;
	⟪(c)⟫ of John the Baptist: ⟦Matthew 21:26|Mt 21:26⟧, ⟦Mark 6:15|Mk 6:15⟧, ⟦Luke 1:76|Lk 1:76⟧;
	⟪(d)⟫ of Christ: ⟦Matthew 21:11|Mt 21:11⟧, ⟦John 6:14|Jo 6:14⟧, ⟦Acts 3:22|Ac 3:22⟧, ⟦Acts 3:23|23⟧ ⟦Acts 7:37|7:37⟧ (LXX);
	⟪(e)⟫ of Christian prophets in the apostolic age: ⟦Acts 15:32|Ac 15:32⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:28|I Co 12:28⟧, ⟦Ephesians 2:20|Eph 2:20⟧, al.;
	⟪(f)⟫ by meton., of the writings of prophets: ⟦Luke 24:27|Lk 24:27⟧, ⟦Acts 8:28|Ac 8:28⟧, al.;
	⟪(g)⟫ of a poet: ⟦Titus 1:12|Tit 1:12⟧ (on the use of the term in π. and Inscr., v. Deiss., BS, 235 f.; MM, xxii).
